      "text": "Given the equations:\n1. \\( ab + bc + cd + da = 30 \\)\n2. \\( b + d = 5 \\)\n\nWe need to find the value of \\( a + c \\).\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the first equation by factoring out common terms:\n\\[ ab + bc + cd + da = b(a + c) + d(a + c) \\]\n\nThis can be factored further:\n\\[ b(a + c) + d(a + c) = (b + d)(a + c) \\]\n\nWe know from the second equation that \\( b + d = 5 \\). Substituting this into the equation, we get:\n\\[ (b + d)(a + c) = 5(a + c) \\]\n\nGiven that \\( ab + bc + cd + da = 30 \\), we substitute back:\n\\[ 5(a + c) = 30 \\]\n\nTo find \\( a + c \\), we solve the equation:\n\\[ a + c = \\frac{30}{5} \\]\n\\[ a + c = 6 \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( a + c \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]",
